---
import Article from '../../layouts/Article.astro'
import AssertionCard from '../../components/AssertionCard.astro'
import ChartFigure from '../../components/ChartFigure.astro'
import DataTable from '../../components/DataTable.astro'
import { assertion } from '../../lib/feeds'
import { bar } from '../../lib/chart-spec'

const libraries = assertion('three-per-cent-of-the-library-money-is-local')

const librarySpec = bar(
  libraries.figures.map((f) => f.label),
  libraries.figures.map((f) => f.value),
  { yTitle: 'Library income by level of government, 2024 (US$)', labelValues: true },
)

const libraryOutlets = [
  ['Lima Public Library', 'Lima', '650 W. Market St.', 60650, 2988],
  ['Delphos Public Library', 'Delphos', '309 W. 2nd St.', 15989, 2496],
  ['Bluffton Public Library', 'Bluffton', '145 S. Main St.', 12874, 2834],
  ['Spencerville branch', 'Spencerville', '2489 Wisher Dr.', 5625, 1872],
  ['Elida branch', 'Elida', '500 E. Kiracofe Ave.', 3990, 1872],
  ['Cairo branch', 'Cairo', '108 Everett Dr.', 1281, 1872],
  ['Lafayette branch', 'Lafayette', '225 E. Sugar St.', 600, 1092],
  ['OSU Lima campus', 'Lima', '4240 Campus Dr.', 100, 2964],
]
---

<Article slug="three-cents-in-the-dollar">
  <AssertionCard assertion={libraries} />
  <p>
    Allen County has three public library systems and eight buildings. Between them they took in
    $6,528,885 in 2024 and $194,728 of it — three per cent — came from local government. Across
    the United States the same column is 85.5 per cent. The county seat's library reports a zero
    in it.
  </p>
  <ChartFigure
    id="library-money"
    title="Allen County public library income by source, 2024"
    caption="Every figure here was reported by the library rather than imputed. 'Other' is a single survey column with no breakdown; for Lima Public Library alone it is $1,603,932, nearly a third of that system's revenue."
    columns={['Source', 'US$']}
    rows={libraries.figures.map((f) => [f.label, f.value])}
  />
  <script type="application/json" data-chart-spec="library-money" set:html={JSON.stringify(librarySpec)} is:inline />
  <p>
    That is a fact about Ohio before it is a fact about Allen County. Ohio pays for its libraries
    from Columbus: the state's 251 systems take 42.9 per cent of their income from the state
    against a national 6.7, and among Ohio's 88 counties Allen is sixteenth from the bottom on the
    local share. Putnam and Shelby report no local money at all.
  </p>
  <p>
    And the money is the same money this page has already counted. The county's own books carry a
    fund called "local government library and township parks" that took in $4,495,636.25 in 2025
    and paid out $4,495,636.25 — one of the fifteen conduits above. Ohio's tax commissioner
    certifies the public library fund to <em>counties</em> and pays it to the county auditor, who
    allocates it. The state's books record a payment to a county, the county's books record a fund
    it does not own, and the library's books record a receipt from the state. Three ledgers, one
    dollar, and no two of these figures may be differenced.
  </p>
  <DataTable
    title="Eight buildings"
    caption="101,109 square feet in all. Every resident of the county is inside exactly one library's legal service area — Lima's covers 88.2 per cent of it, and Bluffton's and Delphos's are school districts that reach over the county line. Beaverdam and Harrod have no outlet."
    columns={['Outlet', 'Town', 'Address', 'Square feet', 'Hours a year']}
    rows={libraryOutlets}
  />
</Article>
